Build a reusable skeleton-loading system for CardVault (React Native + TypeScript + Reanimated), replacing all bare ActivityIndicator usage app-wide.

File: src/components/Skeleton.tsx

Exports:
- <SkeletonBase> — a base rectangle with a shimmer effect: a translateX-animated linear gradient (use react-native-linear-gradient or expo-linear-gradient) sweeping left-to-right over a neutral.100/neutral.200 base, looping every 1200ms via Reanimated's withRepeat(withTiming(...)).
- <SkeletonText lines={n} /> — stacked SkeletonBase bars sized to type.body line-height, last line shorter (70% width) to mimic natural text wrap.
- <SkeletonCard /> — shaped to match the generic Card component's typical content (avatar circle + 2 text lines).
- <SkeletonKPICard /> — shaped to match KPICard (number block + label block).
- <SkeletonSessionCard /> — shaped to match SessionCard.

Integration:
- Update home.tsx to show SkeletonKPICard x3 and SkeletonSessionCard x3 and SkeletonCard x5 (activity feed) while initial data is loading, instead of any ActivityIndicator.
- Update ocr-review.tsx's image-processing step to show a SkeletonCard-shaped placeholder while OCR results are pending, instead of ActivityIndicator.

Requirements:
- TypeScript strict, no `any`.
- Respect reduced-motion: check AccessibilityInfo.isReduceMotionEnabled() and fall back to a static (non-animated) skeleton fill when true.

Acceptance criteria:
- No ActivityIndicator remains in home.tsx or the OCR loading state.
- Skeleton shapes visually match their loaded-state counterparts (same approximate dimensions).
- Shimmer respects the reduced-motion accessibility setting.